"}], "parent_id": "9f91d46d-58c3-4263-8afa-3b9fdc936ca4"}

{"id": "7b8a1538-fb8c-4068-b587-3bbd59897415", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I realize I need the minimum burst balance value rather than the max, so I'll switch to using min() in the query for the remaining batch. I also note one gp3 volume peaked at 125 MiB/s with 500 IOPS before any modification.

The test lab FIS volume is saturated at 98% IOPS with a queue depth of 16, though its instance is stopped. For the next batch I'm checking several more volumes including st1, io2, and gp3 types, and I'll pull both min and max BurstBalance values this time.

"}], "parent_id": "9f91d46d-58c3-4263-8afa-3b9fdc936ca4"}

{"id": "23a8d3ea-61e2-4bae-97af-a33954cf73b2", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I notice i-0cf83fd's EBSIOBalance% dropped to zero, but the burst-credits-low alarm only exists on i-0533, not this instance. I'm also checking the three "ebs-skill-eval" SNS alarms to see what they cover.

Those alarms have no associated actions, one points to a nonexistent instance, and all volumes turn out to be unencrypted. Time to wrap up the findings.

"}], "parent_id": "9f91d46d-58c3-4263-8afa-3b9fdc936ca4"}

